  <section lang="en">
    <h1>iObY Launcher Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>{company.nameEn} ("we", "us") describes below how the application "iObY Launcher" (the "App") handles user information. This policy applies to the Windows version of the App distributed through Microsoft Store.</p>

    <h2>1. Collection and Transmission of Information</h2>
    <p>The App itself does not communicate with our servers. We do not collect any information that identifies you personally. The App contains no mechanisms for advertising or usage analytics (telemetry).</p>
    <p>The App communicates only in the following cases. Each is triggered by your action; the App does not communicate automatically in the background.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Getting icons: when you press "Fetch from site" in the item editor (see section 4)</li>
      <li>AI features: when you translate, use AI chat, or check the connection (see section 3)</li>
      <li>Purchases and license verification: handled through Microsoft Store (see section 5)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>In addition, URLs you registered and web searches are passed to your default browser, and "Report inappropriate response" is passed to your default email app. Any communication after that is handled by those apps. When you open a shared folder you registered, Windows accesses that server through its file sharing system.</p>

    <h2>2. Storage of Settings and Data</h2>
    <p>The App's settings and the items you register are stored on your PC. The App never sends this information to us.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Passwords: encrypted with a key derived from the master password you choose. The master password itself is not stored. The vault locks automatically after a period of inactivity or when you lock Windows.</li>
      <li>Copying passwords: copied passwords are kept out of Windows clipboard history and cloud clipboard sync, and are cleared after a set time.</li>
      <li>AI API keys: stored in a separate file from the settings, encrypted with a Windows feature (DPAPI). They are not included when you export your settings.</li>
      <li>Search window background image (Full Version): a file based on the image you choose is saved in the App's storage area.</li>
      <li>Screenshots: saved only when you take them, to the folder you specify (by default, Screenshots in your Pictures folder). If that folder is synced by a service such as OneDrive, that service's settings apply.</li>
      <li>Exported settings: files you export include your encrypted passwords. Please keep them in a safe place.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. AI Features</h2>
    <p>The App's AI features (translation and AI chat) use an API key that you obtain under your own agreement with an AI provider. Data is sent only to the one provider you choose in Settings:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Google (Gemini API)</li>
      <li>OpenAI</li>
      <li>Anthropic</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The App sends the following, always with your API key and directly to the AI provider. Nothing passes through our servers, and we never receive the content.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Connection check: a short test message</li>
      <li>Translation: the text you enter (up to 5,000 characters) and an instruction that includes the target language</li>
      <li>AI chat: the recent conversation (up to 5 exchanges) and your new message (up to 5,000 characters in total), plus an instruction on how to respond. If you use the Full Version's chat persona, the persona you wrote (up to 300 characters) is sent as that instruction. Without the Full Version, a saved persona is not sent.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Before anything is sent for the first time, the App asks for your confirmation (default: No). Please do not enter confidential business information or personal information. What you send and your use of the API key are handled under each provider's terms and privacy policy and your agreement with that provider (including whether the data is used for training). Usage fees are billed to you by the provider.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Google: <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/terms">Gemini API Terms of Service</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li>OpenAI: <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy">OpenAI Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li>Anthropic: <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy">Anthropic Privacy Policy</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>AI responses may contain errors or inappropriate content. Please tell us about an inappropriate response with "Report inappropriate response" below the response (your email app opens).</p>

    <h2>4. Getting Icons</h2>
    <p>Only when you press "Fetch from site" in the item editor does the App get an icon from the website (http or https) you entered. The icon is saved on your PC as part of that item.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The App sends only requests to load the page and the icon. It does not send cookies, login credentials, or the referrer.</li>
      <li>As with ordinary web browsing, the website receives information such as your IP address.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Purchases and License Verification</h2>
    <p>Purchases of and payments for the App and the add-on "iObY Launcher Full Version", and license verification, are processed by Microsoft Store. We never receive your payment information or purchase records. Related information is handled in accordance with Microsoft's policies (<a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/en-us/privacystatement">Microsoft Privacy Statement</a>).</p>
    <p>The App uses the result received from Microsoft Store only to decide whether the Full Version features are available. The result is not saved to any file or setting; the App checks again each time it starts.</p>

    <h2>6. Components Used to Display the App</h2>
    <p>The App uses the Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime to render its display. This component operates in accordance with Microsoft's policies (for example, runtime updates and Windows diagnostic data settings). The App turns off WebView2's URL reputation checks (SmartScreen).</p>

    <h2>7. Children</h2>
    <p>We do not collect information that identifies you personally, regardless of your age. If you use the AI features, please follow each AI provider's terms of use (including any age requirements).</p>

    <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>If we revise this policy, we will announce the changes on this page.</p>

    <h2>9. Operator and Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Operator: {company.nameEn}<br />
      Contact: <a href={`mailto:${contact.supportEmail}`}>{contact.supportEmail}</a>
    </p>

    <p>Last updated: {updatedEn}</p>
  </section>
